Z||000000||Formula||10-10-1999||03:31 PM||||a local mechanic said that my engine has a main bearing thats about ready to go. It started knocking today. How much do you think this is to fix and is it cheaper to buy  the rebuilt motor||||reg||1
Z||000001||batboy||10-10-1999||07:53 PM||||If it is a bad main bearing, that basically means a complete rebuild to fix it. There's a chance that it's a rod bearing instead, but that means the same thing too, a complete rebuild. If this is an everyday driver and you don't want to do any performance mods, then a good remanufactured engine might be a cheaper route to go, depending on what's all wrong with your present engine.<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 10-10-1999).]||||reg||1
